% 1-object: a function runs once for each object its first argument may
% be (Milanova's receiver). A call with none keeps its caller's context.
% The first parameter then holds that object alone, the "filter" that
% makes a method's this precise.
%
% (A first argument with no object in this context: no run gets here, every
% value having one, a scalar at least: Closure_facts and Facts. Not quite, for
% C: what is read from a global or a field never written, 0, has none, so a
% call given that is not followed. tests/hole.c, tests/dynamic.sh -c.)
filtered(I) :- has_object(I).
callee(I, C1, C2, F, O, none) :-
  passed(I, 1, C1, C2, O, _, _), has_object(I), fresh(I, C1, C2, F, _, _).
callee(I, C1, C2, F, C1, C2) :- fresh(I, C1, C2, F, _, _), \+ has_object(I).
flow(P, O, none, O, O1, O2) :-
  passed(I, 1, C1, C2, O, O1, O2), filtered(I),
  callee(I, C1, C2, F, O, none), parameter(F, 1, P).
flow(V, C1, C2, H, none, none) :- new_site(V, H, C1, C2).
